 "chapter": "Cliffhanger",
 "topic": "What if you had an iPhone 100 years ago?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "the decision",
   "text": "You walk downstairs. You put the phone on the table. The man reaches for it."
  },
  {
   "beat": "the impossible",
   "text": "And it buzzes. One bar of signal. In 1926. Which is impossible. Unless someone else is here too."
  },
  {
   "beat": "the message",
   "text": "A message appears. 'Don't give it to him.' One percent. And the screen goes black."
  },
  {
   "beat": "the laugh",
   "text": "In the dark, you hear the man in the grey suit laugh, very softly. 'Well,' he says. 'That changes things.'"
  },
  {
   "beat": "added: still awake",
   "text": "Mo grabs your sleeve. Upstairs, Ellie coughs in her sleep. And on the table, the dead phone is warm, as if something inside it is still awake."
  },
  {
   "beat": "question",
   "text": "So what would you do? Save Ellie, or save the future? Tell me in the comments."
  },
  {
   "beat": "is any of this real",
   "text": "And is any of this real? The rules are. No cell network until 1979. No GPS until 1978. No penicillin until 1928. A hundred years ago, a computer was a person with a pencil. And whoever sent that message? You'll find out in part two."
  }
 ],
